%I A399566 #28 Oct 13 2026 14:58:48
%S A399566 8,10,12,4,8,23,0,12,16,18,8,16,0,8,20,14,0,40,0,14,16,10,8,22,0,8,20,
%T A399566 10,8,53,0,8,20,0,8,41,0,0,8,24,8,32,0,12,28,10,0,41,0,24,8,10,8,61,
%U A399566 16,12,0,10,0,53,0,0,24,8,8,33,0,8,20
%N A399566 Number of k such that A046073(k) = n.
%C A399566 If the multiplicative group of integers modulo k is of the form C_{2m_1} X ... X C_{2m_r}, with m_1 | m_2 | ... | m_r, then the number of squares modulo k is A046073(k) = m_1*...*m_r. In particular, any k with A046073(k) = n must divide A079612(2*n).
%C A399566 For squarefree n > 1, A046073(k) = n if and only if the multiplicative group of integers modulo k is of the form (C_2)^r X C_{2n} (cf. A400852).
%C A399566 a(n) != 0 is not equivalent to n in A396684: 175 is not a term in A396684, but a(175) != 0 (the corresponding k satisfying (Z/kZ)* = (C_2)^r X C_10 X C_70); 182 is a term in A396684, but a(182) = 0 (there are no k satisfying (Z/kZ)* = (C_2)^r X C_364).
%C A399566 a(n) is divisible by 4 for odd n: A046073(k) = n if and only if k = k', 2*k', 4*k', or 8*k' where k' is an odd number such that A046073(m) = n.
%C A399566 a(n) is even for n not divisible by 3: A046073(k) = n if and only if k = k' or 3*k' where k' is a number not divisible by 3 such that A046073(m) = n.
%C A399566 a(n) is divisible by 8 if n is divisible neither by 2 nor by 3.
%H A399566 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399566/b399566.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1889</a>
%H A399566 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399566/a399566.txt">List of k such that A046073(k) = n <= 1889</a>.
%e A399566 a(4) = 4: If the number of squares in (Z/kZ)* is 4, then (Z/kZ)* is of the form either (C_2)^r X C_8 or (C_2)^r X C_4 X C_4. We have k = 32, 96 in the former case and k = 80, 240 in the latter case.
%e A399566 a(68) = 8: If the number of squares in (Z/kZ)* is 68, then (Z/kZ)* is of the form either (C_2)^r X C_136 or (C_2)^r X C_4 X C_68. In the former case we have k = 137*d with d being a divisor of 24, and the latter case is impossible.
%e A399566 a(98) = 8: If the number of squares in (Z/kZ)* is 98, then (Z/kZ)* is of the form either (C_2)^r X C_196 or (C_2)^r X C_14 X C_28. In the former case we have k = 197*d with d being a divisor of 24, and the latter case is impossible.
%o A399566 (PARI) v(n) = select(x->A046073(x)==n, divisors(A079612(2*n))); \\ Gives the list of k such that A046073(k) = n; see A046073 and A079612 for their PARI programs. Warning: This is very inefficient since A079612(2*n) can easily have tens of millions of divisors. For squarefree n, it is much more advised to use multgp() given in the link of the PARI program for A400852.
%o A399566 A399566(n) = #v(n);
%Y A399566 Cf. A046073, A079612, A396684, A400852.
%Y A399566 Cf. A400862, A400854, A400855.
%K A399566 nonn,new
%O A399566 1,1
